      "content": "The debate centers on whether the Second Amendment guarantees an individual right to keep and bear arms constrained by historical context (originalism) or one that evolves with modern societal needs (living constitutionalism). Originalists argue that the Constitution's text and 18th-century history provide clear limits on government power regarding gun ownership. Conversely, living constitutionalists contend that the text is a framework for current interpretations, potentially requiring a more comprehensive right to possess firearms for all lawful purposes. This conflict fuels ongoing legal arguments about the scope and regulation of firearms in the United States.",
